I’ll inspect the diffraction data and metadata first, then identify candidate phases, refine them jointly in GSAS-II, and validate the exported CIFs, phase fractions, profile, and project against one another. I’ll flag any ambiguity that the pattern cannot resolve.

The chemistry points strongly toward a nickel tungstate, but I’m treating residual oxides or polymorphs as open possibilities. The scan is high-resolution (0.01087° steps, 9.90–100.09° 2θ) with a substantial raw background, so I’m separating peak positions from background before committing to a phase model.

Peak matching now supports three crystalline phases: monoclinic NiWO₄, monoclinic WO₃, and rocksalt NiO. Their diagnostic lines recur across the full scan—for example NiWO₄ at about 19.28/30.9/36.58°, WO₃ at 23.14/23.56/24.37/33.28°, and NiO at 37.34/43.42/63.08/75.54°. I’m moving to a joint three-phase refinement; this also tests whether any significant peaks remain unassigned.

The joint refinement explains the peak positions and intensities without an extra crystalline phase. Refining the two low-symmetry structures’ coordinates (while keeping NiO symmetry-fixed) reduced \(R_{wp}\) from about 4.4% to 1.79%, close to the counting-statistics limit of 1.45%; refined metal–oxygen distances remain chemically sensible. I’m now stabilizing the covariance model and checking exports and normalized weight fractions.

The converged model gives 60.06 wt% NiWO₄, 30.26 wt% WO₃, and 9.68 wt% NiO on a crystalline-only basis. The fit is statistically close to the Poisson limit (\(R_{wp}=1.788\%\), GOF 1.240). I’ve generated all requested artifacts from the delivered `final.gpx`; I’m doing a final cross-check that the project, CIF cells/compositions, profile columns, JSON fractions, and statistics agree exactly.

Completed the three-phase GSAS-II refinement:

- NiWO₄: 60.059 ± 0.031 wt%
- WO₃: 30.260 ± 0.027 wt%
- NiO: 9.681 ± 0.029 wt%

Final fit: \(R_{wp}=1.788\%\), \(R_p=1.350\%\), GOF = 1.240. Fractions are normalized over modeled crystalline phases; amorphous content remains undetermined.

